 {"id": "DF-BOARDCTL-23", "type": null, "status": "complete", "priority": "P3", "title": "vulncheck version pin skips a binary whose -version output has no parsable 'Scanner:' line — a stub or reimplementation defeats the pin by staying silent", "reasoning": "Run-18 boundary probe on wt/BT-064's fix (9393ed0): CheckVersion correctly refuses a parseable wrong version ('Scanner: govulncheck@v0.0.9' -> gate FAIL rc=2 naming expected v1.7.0 / actual v0.0.9), but a stub that prints a version banner WITHOUT the exact 'Scanner: govulncheck@' prefix is treated as absent and the gate proceeds green (proven: a stub echoing 'govulncheck@v0.0.9' makes make vuln-check rc=0). The skip is deliberate and documented in CheckVersion's doc comment ('PATH-fallback behavior unchanged'), and real govulncheck prints the line, so the practical risk is wrappers/reimplementations — but refusing exactly those is the pin's point. Fix direction: when the binary exists and -version exits 0 yet yields no Scanner line, at least WARN (or fail behind an explicit override env) instead of silently passing.", "detail": {"fingerprint": "2c46b72e95b8cdeeba93737e572fc69eb613dc4bf83ea113735088ece41e5c3d"}, "created_at": "2026-09-29T10:29:36Z", "created_by": null, "worker_status": "complete", "commit_hash": "8671d10", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": null, "capability_tags": ["gates", "supply-chain"], "complexity": 2, "updated_at": "2026-09-29T11:20:00Z", "worker_summary": "merged to main beeabbc; tier-2 verdict PASS; worktree reaped", "foreman_note": null, "completed_at": "2026-09-29T11:35:00Z", "worktree": null, "branch": null, "sessions": null}
