 {"id": "BT-070", "type": null, "status": "complete", "priority": "P2", "title": "boardctl priority vocabulary is P0..P3 — extend it to P0..P5 (Bane 2026-09-30)", "reasoning": "BANE 2026-09-30 (verbatim): \"boardctl needs a task added to it that it supports upto P5.\"\n\nToday the canonical on-disk priority vocabulary is {P0,P1,P2,P3}:\n- internal/board/validate.go:168 — the BT-048 PriorityVocabulary map + the \"not in vocabulary {P0,P1,P2,P3}\" warning text (lines 180/183).\n- internal/board/validate.go:392 — `titlePriorityToken = regexp.MustCompile(`(^|[^A-Za-z0-9])([Pp][0-3])([^A-Za-z0-9]|$)`)` (title-vs-field drift detection is P0-P3 only).\n- NormalizePriority — accepts bare `0`..`3` (and case variants) → canonical Pn.\n- internal/render/load.go:480 + internal/render/template.go:812 — `priorityLabel` documents the read-side rule as \"string form as-is (P0..P3)\".\n- create/update `--priority` flag validates against the same set.\n\nExtend the vocabulary to {P0..P5}.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n1. `boardctl create|update --priority P4` and `--priority P5` are accepted; P0..P3 behaviour unchanged.\n2. Validation treats P4/P5 as in-vocabulary; the warning/error text naming the set reads {P0..P5}.\n3. NormalizePriority maps bare `4`/`5` → P4/P5 (mirrors the 0-3 rule).\n4. `titlePriorityToken` matches P0..P5, so title-carries-Pn/field-mismatch drift is caught for P4/P5 too.\n5. The render label + any ordering/rank map is TOTAL across P0..P5 (P4/P5 sort AFTER P3 in every list/queue view).\n6. Tests for each of 1-5; help text updated.\n\nWHY: the paperwork satellites (see the companion task) need P4/P5 to sit at the end of the queue — and the tool must accept the value before any lane can carry it.", "detail": {"fingerprint": "90b03dce768adedfd8ac7d401ac5581bce281ba74475dd0cae156d84399de646"}, "created_at": "2026-10-01T00:34:05Z", "created_by": null, "worker_status": "complete", "commit_hash": "bf46263", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "PASS", "capability_tags": ["b